.TH ckman-oath-accounts-rename 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-oath\-accounts\-rename \- Rename an account
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-oath\-accounts\-rename\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-remember\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIQUERY\fR> <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename an account
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Do not ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
The password to unlock the OATH application
.TP
\fB\-\-remember\fR
Remember the access key on this machine (long\-only: the global \-r/\-\-reader owns the short flag)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIQUERY\fR>
A query to match a single account (as shown in "list")
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
The new name of the account (use "issuer:name" to specify an issuer)
